  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Friday)\nIssued at 1039 PM CDT Fri Sep 25 2026\n\nOverall, the pattern will be in transition this period after a weak\ntrough pushes into the Southeast U.S. Tuesday, being overwhelmed by a\nbuilding ridge over the southwest Atlantic basin. This builds\ninfluence into the southeast U.S. Wednesday and Thursday. While in\nthe southwest U.S. and Plains, a complex upper low and eventual remnant\nHurricane Polo evolution remain uncertain. For our area, southerly\nflow will be enhanced between the ridge and trough, keeping moist and\nunstable air flow northward. This will introduce low chances of\nshowers and thunderstorms, primarily daytime heating driven, during\nthe latter half of next week. Temperatures will also be on a warming\ntrend with highs in the upper 80s to lower 90s.",
